  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "Suppose that \\((u_n)\\) is a sequence of real numbers satisfying \\(u_{n+2}=2u_{n+1}+u_n,\\) and that \\(u_3=9\\) and \\(u_6=128.\\) What is \\(u_5?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(40\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(53\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(68\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(88\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(104\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "53"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2008-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using the recurrence, \\(u_5=2u_4+u_3=2u_4+9\\) and \\(u_6=2u_5+u_4\\) \\(=2(2u_4+9)+u_4\\) \\(=5u_4+18.\\)\n\nSetting \\(5u_4+18=128\\) gives \\(u_4=22,\\) so \\(u_5=2\\cdot 22+9=53.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Write \\(u_5\\) and \\(u_6\\) in terms of \\(u_4\\) and \\(u_3\\)",
        "\\(u_5=2u_4+9\\) and \\(u_6=2u_5+u_4,\\) so \\(128=5u_4+18\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
